meta {
  name: Get Tenant Locale
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/tenant/locale
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Returns the caller tenant's identity + locale so the business frontend can
  label the active business (name + address), convert UTC timestamps into business-local time,
  and format money with the configured currency. Protected by the business JWT
  (any authenticated business user); scoped to the caller's own tenant from the
  token — no id in the path.

  Response `data`:
  - `businessName` — the tenant's display name (`Tenant.name`); used e.g. as the
    org-wide group label in the profile switcher.
  - `businessAddress` — the tenant's registered address as one line (e.g.
    `12 MG Road, Indiranagar, Bengaluru, Karnataka, 560038, India`): address
    line → area → city → state → pincode → country, blanks skipped. Tenants
    without the structured fields fall back to the legacy free-form `address`
    JSON; `""` when no address is stored. Used e.g. in exported report headers.
  - `timezone` — IANA time zone (e.g. `Asia/Kolkata`). Always one of the
    supported zones; an unsupported stored value falls back to the platform
    default `Asia/Kolkata`.
  - `currency` — ISO 4217 code (e.g. `INR`).
  - `dateFormat` — display date format (e.g. `DD/MM/YYYY`).
  - `timeFormat` — display clock style (`12h` or `24h`).
  - `language` — UI language (e.g. `en`).

  Storage is unchanged: all timestamps remain UTC in the DB; this endpoint only
  supplies the zone/currency used at display time.
}
